@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;build;verification] native-promotion-exact-reviewed-artifacts
Promotion MUST verify the shared protocol's exact native image ID, positive
kernel provenance, actual firmware and raw disk bytes, the reviewed VMM digest,
and hash-bound assembly and five native scenario evidence sets before writing
manifest.json. Missing, foreign, stale or incomplete evidence MUST refuse.
Candidate and kit constructors MUST retain their own false admission flags.
Promotion MUST NOT imply physical isolation, power-loss durability or fleet
acceptance beyond the explicitly reviewed machine evidence.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;deployment] native-published-candidate-custody
A manually assembled candidate MUST enter Nix through a reviewed recursive NAR
hash and be published through the existing signature-verified Overalls cache.
A cache miss MUST refuse with publication instructions, never read an ephemeral
host path, rebuild a stock disk or disable signature checks. No cache credential
or private signing key may enter the constructor or guest artifact.
